<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Shelley returns three weeks after a left frontoparietal craniotomy. The tumor was removed completely with its dural attachment and a margin of dura (Simpson grade I), and the MRI the next day showed no residual tumor. The pathology is a meningothelial meningioma, CNS WHO grade 1: one mitosis per ten high-power fields, no brain invasion, no atypical features, Ki-67 3 percent, and no TERT promoter mutation or CDKN2A/B deletion. Her right hand was weaker for the first two days after surgery and has been improving steadily. She took dexamethasone for three days before surgery and stopped the taper eleven days ago. She has had no seizure since starting levetiracetam six weeks ago. She notices that she is short-tempered and tearful at times, which she links to the tablets as much as to the operation, and she has seen the counselor twice. The wound has healed and the staples are out. She has begun to write for half an hour a day. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Surgery</td><td>Simpson grade I resection; gross total on MRI the next day</td></tr><tr><td>Pathology</td><td>Meningothelial meningioma, CNS WHO grade 1</td></tr><tr><td>Seizures</td><td>None since starting levetiracetam</td></tr><tr><td>Steroid</td><td>Dexamethasone stopped eleven days ago</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>Irritable and tearful at times; two counselor sessions</td></tr><tr><td>Writing</td><td>Half an hour a day</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

