<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Meningioma, CNS WHO grade 1, after Simpson grade I resection (D32.0)</content>. Complete resection of a grade 1 meningioma; the risk of recurrence is low, and radiation would add harm without clear benefit, so none is given. Glucose 96 mg/dL and sodium 138 mmol/L after the steroid course; hemoglobin 12.1 g/dL. [S]<list><item>No radiation.</item><item>MRI with gadolinium at three months, then yearly for five years, then every two years.</item><item>Occupational therapy for fine hand movements, twice a week for four weeks.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Focal epilepsy on levetiracetam (G40.109)</content>. Seizure-free for six weeks. PHQ-9 9 with irritability that may be a levetiracetam effect. Options discussed: continue and watch, a lower dose, or a switch to another medicine such as lacosamide. She chose to continue for now, because the seizures stopped and she does not want a change before the three-month scan. [S]<list><item>Continue levetiracetam 500 mg twice a day for at least a year after surgery.</item><item>Call if irritability or low mood worsens, or at once for any thoughts of self-harm; the switch remains open.</item><item>No driving yet.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>MRI within 48 hours after surgery</td><td>Within 48 hours of resection</td><td>Up to date</td><td>The day after surgery: gross total resection</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>WHO CNS5 grading of the resected tumor (mitoses, brain invasion, histological subtype, TERT promoter, CDKN2A/B)</td><td>On the surgical specimen</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Meningothelial meningioma, CNS WHO grade 1; no TERT promoter mutation or CDKN2A/B deletion</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Radiation oncology</td><td>After resection of grade 2 or 3 tumors, or incomplete resection with symptoms</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Grade 1 after Simpson grade I resection</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Glucose and sodium after corticosteroid and craniotomy</td><td>After a steroid course and intracranial surgery</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Glucose 96 mg/dL, sodium 138 mmol/L, hemoglobin 12.1 g/dL</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Corticosteroid stopped as soon as possible</td><td>Shortest course</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dexamethasone stopped eleven days ago after a ten-day taper</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Seizure diary, triggers (sleep loss, alcohol, missed doses), and seizure first aid</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No seizures since levetiracetam was started; regular sleep kept</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>PHQ-9, with a question about irritability on levetiracetam</td><td>Every visit while on levetiracetam and during cancer treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>9, with irritability and tearfulness; two counselor sessions; continuing levetiracetam by her choice with a low threshold to switch</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>GAD-7</td><td>Every visit during the diagnostic and treatment phase</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Missed at the second visit and again today; the PHQ-9 was done each time and the counselor is assessing anxiety, so no harm is judged to have resulted. Corrective action: the GAD-7 is added to the visit template and will be done at the next visit</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Driving</td><td>Until seizure-free for the state&apos;s required period and cleared after craniotomy</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Not driving</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Occupational therapy for hand function</td><td>If weakness persists after surgery</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Twice a week for four weeks</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>A diagnosis within two weeks, explained in plain words with the images and reports. Outcome by 1849-03-17: MRI and EEG within a week; diagnosis explained at two weeks with the images [S]</item><item>No further seizures. In progress; target 1850-04-07 [S]</item><item>Full use of the right hand and return to writing every morning. In progress; target 1849-09-29 [S]</item><item>Decide on treatment herself after hearing the options, benefits, and harms. Outcome by 1849-03-17: Chose resection after observation and radiosurgery were explained [S]</item><item>Mood and grief supported: PHQ-9 below 5 and a counselor available. In progress; target 1849-09-29 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: EANO guideline on the diagnosis and management of meningiomas. Goldbrunner R, et al. Neuro Oncol 2021;23(11):1821-1834 (2021); NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Central Nervous System Cancers, Version 2.2025 (2025); Evidence-based guideline: Management of an unprovoked first seizure in adults. Krumholz A, et al. Neurology 2015;84(16):1705-1713 (2015); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (depression screening and PHQ-9 follow-up) (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Occupational therapy twice a week; counselor fortnightly; MRI at three months and review a few days later. Next scheduled visit 1849-07-07: three-month MRI review after resection. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
